 `--scenario play` draws the game world held by `hex-app` (`crates/hex-app/src/game.rs`). It opens with one meadow at `(0, 0)` and follows the PRD §4.1–4.2 rules from `hex-core`. Tiles use kit pieces from `assets/kit/manifest.json` where the tile references them and the piece's pack has loaded (see [Kit streaming](#kit-streaming)), and plain placeholders otherwise: a coloured prism per biome, dark road and blue river strips meeting at a hub, and beige blocks for pending houses, pads and hero props.
 
-Hero variants (PRD §6 Variety): a hero slot authored as a piece listed in `hex_core::HERO_VARIANTS` may draw one of its variants instead, picked by `hex_core::hero_piece(def, cell, slot)` from a SplitMix64 hash of the cell and the slot index. Today a `house_cottage` slot draws `house_longhouse` or `house_cottage_b` (slate roof, gabled porch, a stack at each gable), the `house_twostorey` slot draws `house_twostorey_b` (jettied, hip-roofed), and the oak tile's `tree_hero_oak` slot draws `tree_hero_oak_b` (forked, east-leaning, a heavy low limb), each slot varying about one time in three (`VARIANT_ONE_IN`); a slot with several variants splits that share evenly (`variants[(h / 3) % n]`), so a cottage slot keeps the cottage two times in three and draws each variant about one time in six, and a house cluster shows any two of the three cottage designs beside a two-storey of either kind. The pick depends on the cell alone, so saves carry nothing for it and a ghost previews the same houses the placed tile draws. Every consumer of a hero piece resolves it through `TileDef::hero_pieces(cell)`: the drawn tile, the ghost, walk obstacles and photo picks, grass exclusions and bird perches. The pack loader and scatter masks, which are per tile and not per cell, take every option of a slot (`TileDef::hero_options`; scatter clears the widest). `hex_core::VARIANT_PICK` switches the rule to one pick per cluster (`PerCluster`) or a fixed slot (`FixedSlot(n)`). `cargo test -p hex-core longhouse_cells -- --ignored --nocapture` prints the picks near the origin. The thumbnail cell, the origin, draws both cottages and `house_twostorey_b`, and the authored `tree_hero_oak`. Evidence: `docs/checkpoints/house_cottage_b/cottage_b-play-overview.jpg`, four clusters around the start meadow at (1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, -1) and (-1, 1); the first three draw `house_cottage_b` in one cottage slot and (-1, 1) draws `house_longhouse`, from `caffeinate -d -u target/release/hex-world --scenario play --script docs/checkpoints/house_cottage_b/play.json --size 1600x1000 --seed 1 --fps off --tilt off --clock fixed`, which also takes a walk-mode eye-level shot in the (1, 0) yard (`cottage_b-walk-eye.jpg`). The older `docs/checkpoints/house_longhouse/play.jpg` and `play-overview.jpg` show the same four cells before `house_cottage_b` joined the row, each with one longhouse.
